Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.

As an Electrotechnician, you will play a key role in ensuring the reliability and safety of electrical systems. You will work on installation projects, perform maintenance activities, and troubleshoot technical issues to keep operations running smoothly.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing electrical systems and equipment;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations to ensure compliance with safety regulations;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Collaborating with colleagues and customers to deliver high-quality solutions.

This is a varied position where no two days are the same, offering plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills.

- MBO Level 3 diploma in Electrical Engineering or a comparable technical qualification;
- Minimum of 2 years of experience as an Electrotechnician;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B is considered an advantage;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong focus on safety, quality, and precision;
- Ability to work independently as well as part of a team.

As a C Driver, you are responsible for driving the truck and delivering a wide range of food and non-food products to customers such as restaurants, cafés, sports clubs, and company canteens. Together with your driver’s assistant, you handle loading and unloading and ensure deliveries are completed safely and efficiently.

This is an active role where you are frequently on the move and work in all weather conditions. You will primarily work from Monday to Friday, with regular shifts on Saturdays. Your start time is fixed, but flexibility is required regarding your finishing time.

At the start of the day, you review the route together, load the truck, and begin your deliveries. You also handle basic administrative tasks and provide friendly, customer-focused service. After completing your route, you return to the depot and check in for any additional assignments.

If you perform well, you will have the opportunity to obtain your CE license and grow within the company.

- Valid Category C driving licence and Code 95;
- In possession of a digital driver card;
- Own transport (car/moped/scooter/motorcycle);
- Experience as a driver;
- Living in the vicinity of Berkel en Rodenrijs;
- Presentable appearance;
- Available full-time and flexible;
- Good command of the English language, both spoken and written;

From the job description, you may have already noticed that this is a physically demanding role in which you do more than just drive the vehicle. It is therefore important that this suits you. If so, we encourage you to apply. Who knows, you might soon start working for our client.

As a loader, you’ll hit the road with the driver and fellow loaders to collect waste in the Eindhoven, Geldrop-Mierlo, and Valkenswaard regions.

What will you be doing?

- Emptying containers (gray, green, blue, and underground)
- Neatly returning containers to their proper places
- Noting any unusual occurrences in the neighborhood
- Ensuring safe and efficient teamwork
- Contributing to clean and well-maintained streets

You’ll work between 07:30 and 16:00 (Monday through Friday). The number of hours is flexible: from 8 to 40 hours per week. Together, we’ll figure out what works best for you.

- You are physically fit and strong;
- You enjoy working outdoors, in all kinds of weather;
- You speak Dutch or English well;
- You have a Class B driver's license;

SamenvattingAre you handy, do you enjoy working with electronics, and do you have an eye for quality? Then we are looking for production employees in Bleiswijk to help dismantle, clean, test, and assemble returned products. Good work!Over de functieIn this role, you will work with returned equipment and be responsible for:
dismantling modems, routers, and components;
cleaning parts and devices;
testing components and complete products;
assembling refurbished devices;
accurately recording test results.

At this company, you will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:30 to 16:30.
Over het bedrijfThe company you will be working for provides integrated logistics solutions with a strong focus on sustainability and circularity. They process returns efficiently and help customers maximize the value and usability of their devices.
Wat wij vragenYou are energetic and able to stay on your feet throughout a full working day;
You have an interest in electronics and technical tasks;
You have a good command of English;
You work accurately and perform well in a team.

Wat wij biedenAn attractive gross hourly wage of €15.26;
8.33% holiday allowance and 25 paid vacation days per year;
Travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre;
A strong chance of receiving a permanent contract after 6 months;
Realistic opportunities for growth and development;
A pleasant working environment within a fast-growing organisation.

Meer informatieAre you ready to start as a production employee in Bleiswijk? You can apply in as little as 2 minutes.
Do you have any questions? Our team will be happy to assist you at +31 10 322 0177 or via denhaag-west@carriere.com
